# Wave W17-AC (Route 229): loop rock — headland rock: a grey-green jointed boulder standing in the loop lane, foam collar at its base — the headland’s foot where the lane turns (design: the lane loops wide around the island’s south point; the rocks are the point’s own teeth). The baked water is the shipped sea entire — the register is carried by the boulder’s headland face, never by a mismatched water square. Route 229’s own rock — split from its twin Route 230’s harbour rock by face entire (grey-green headland vs warm harbour brown) and from Route 220’s swell rock by jointing: headland-struck here, swell-worn there.
